{
  "id": "2026-10-04-kidney-100th-birthday",
  "title": "A man's kidney just turned 100, and it's still going strong",
  "topic": "일상",
  "level": 2,
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
  "sentences": [
    "Good morning!",
    "Here's a birthday story with a twist.",
    "Ray Vetuskey, a man from upstate New York, is celebrating the hundredth birthday of his kidney.",
    "The kidney is a hundred because it used to belong to his mother, Betty.",
    "In 1978, when Ray was sixteen, his kidneys failed, and he had to go on dialysis.",
    "Betty, who was fifty-two at the time, offered him one of hers without a second thought.",
    "Ray remembers being more worried about a concert he didn't want to miss than about the surgery itself.",
    "Most kidneys from living donors last fifteen to twenty years.",
    "Ray's has been working for forty-eight.",
    "That makes him the longest-surviving kidney recipient in the history of his hospital in Rochester.",
    "Betty has since passed away, but a part of her is still keeping her son alive.",
    "Doctors say a close family match can make a real difference, and his kidney may well last for the rest of his life.",
    "These days, Ray only needs one check-up a year.",
    "To honor his mother, he even named a star after her.",
    "If you have a minute today, call someone who once did something big for you, and tell them you still remember."
  ],
  "summary_ko": [
    "1978년 16세에 신부전이 온 레이에게 52세 어머니 베티가 신장 하나를 망설임 없이 내줬다.",
    "보통 생체 기증 신장은 15~20년 가는데, 이 신장은 48년째 작동해 병원 역사상 최장 기록이다.",
    "어머니는 세상을 떠났지만 올해 그 신장이 100살이 됐고, 레이는 어머니 이름을 별에 붙였다."
  ],
